@trap
**Etawah 1948, Albert Mayer.** **CDP 2 October 1952, S.K. Dey.** **TRYSEM 1979, NREP 1980, JRY 1989, EAS 1993, SGSY 1999, SGRY 2001, NRLM 2011.** **SGSY did not include JRY.** **MGNREGA: 2 February 2006, 200 districts → country 1 April 2008; 100 days per household; replaced by VB-G RAM G (125 days, 2025).** **Jan Dhan 28 August 2014.** **Ujjwala 1 May 2016, Ballia.** **PAHAL = Guinness DBT.** **Saubhagya = electricity.** **RIDF = NABARD 1995-96.** **JJM 2019.** **Swachh Bharat ≠ drinking water.** **Rurban Mission 2016.** **AMRUT: 500 cities, 60% urban population.** **Sugamya Bharat & Sangam = disabled.**
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
Scheme chronology questions are now the norm: the **2024 and 2025** Prelims asked four "arrange in order" questions on rural programmes and missions. MGNREGA and Swachh Bharat facts recur every few years.
@end

@next
Likely next angles: the **VB-G RAM G Act** (125 days) replacing MGNREGA, **Jal Jeevan Mission** extension to 2028, **PMAY-G** till 2029, **SBM-Gramin** ODF Plus, **Swachh Survekshan 2024-25** (Super Swachh League), **Lakhpati Didi**, and **UP's** ranks in these schemes.
@end
